  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday morning through next Friday)\nIssued at 300 PM EDT Sat Sep 26 2026\n\nPleasant conditions will start off the long term as we begin the \nwork week. Temperatures in the upper 80s and lower 90s for much of \nthe CWA as the high pressure begins to break down and winds become \nmore southerly. \n\nAs we approach the weekend, the ridge will begin to break down and \nsoutherly flow will begin to pull moisture back into the CWA. This \nwill bring chances for thunderstorms back up to between 25-35% \nduring the afternoon, though temperatures should remain moderated \nto the upper 80s and lower 90s. While widespread severe weather \ndoens't appear likely this weekend given the weak dynamics out a \nhead of a strong low, we'll need to keep an eye on early next week\nas a more potent trough exits the southwest.",
